[Ip]
Name=ADC
Version=aditf5_v2_1_Cube

[Parameters]
# имя|подпись|группа|единица|мин|макс|описание
SubFamily|SubFamily|ADCGroup||||
master|Master Flag|||0|1|
UnUsedParameter|UnUsedParameter|||||
FadcConstraint|Fadc Constraint|||140000|26000000|
Mode|Mode|ADCsgroup||||Multi ADC mode selection: Configures the ADC to operate in independent or multi mode
DMAAccessModeView|DMA Access Mode|ADCsgroup||||
DMAAccessMode|DMA Access Mode|ADCsgroup||||
TwoSamplingDelay|Delay between 2 sampling phases|ADCsgroup||||Delay between 2 sampling phases
ClockPrescaler|Clock Prescaler|ADCsgroup||||frequency of the clock to the ADC. The clock is common for all the ADCs.
Resolution|Resolution|ADCGroup||||Resolution of the ADC conversion
DataAlign|Data Alignment|ADCGroup||||Select the alignment of the data stored after conversion.
ScanConvMode|Scan Conversion Mode|ADCgroup||||Enable or Disable the Scan Conversion Mode , To enable Scan conversion Mode : the number of Conversion should be > 1
ContinuousConvMode|Continuous Conversion Mode|ADCGroup||||Enable or Disable the Continuous Conversion Mode
DiscontinuousConvMode|Discontinuous Conversion Mode|ADCGroup||||Discontinuous Conversion Mode
NbrOfDiscConversion|Number Of Discontinuous Conversions|ADCgroup||1|8|
DMAContinuousRequests|DMA Continuous Requests|ADCgroup||||This parameter is used only when a DMA Request is configured. Else it is not relevant. When the DMA Request for this ADC instance this parameter specifies whether the DMA requests are performed in one shot mode (DMA transfer stops when number of conversions is reached) or are performed in continuous mode (DMA transfer unlimited, whatever number of conversions). Note: In continuous mode, DMA must be configured in circular mode. Otherwise an overrun will be triggered when DMA buffer maximum pointer is reached.
DMAContinuousRequestsForConfigFile|DMA Continuous Requests|ADCGroup||||Enable/Disable DMA Continuous Requests
EOCSelection|End Of Conversion Selection|ADCGroup||||Regular channel end of conversion selection
Overrun|Overrun behaviour|ADCGroup||||Select the behaviour in case of overrun
LowPowerAutoWait|Low Power Auto Wait|ADCGroup||||Specifies the usage of Low Power Auto Wait Mode: new conversion start only when the previous conversion (for regular group) or previous sequence (for injected group) has been treated by user software.
EnableRegularConversion|Enable Regular Conversions|ADCgroup||||Enable/Disable Regular Conversion
NbrOfConversionFlag|Number Of Conversion Flag|ADCGroup||0|1|
NbrOfConversion|Number Of Conversion|ADCGroup||1|16|Number of regular channels to be converted
commmn|comm|||||
ChannelVREF|ChannelVREF|||||
ChannelTS|ChannelTS|||||
ChannelVBAT|Channelvbat|||||
ExternalTrigConv|External Trigger Conversion Source|ADCgroup||||Select the external event used to trigger the start of conversion of a regular group
ExternalTrigConvEdge|External Trigger Conversion Edge|ADCGroup||||Select the external trigger polarity and enable the trigger of a regular group: When an external trigger is selected for ADC regular or injected conversion, only the rising edge of the signal can start the conversion.
Rank|Rank|ADCChannel||1|16|The rank in the regular group sequencer
OffsetNumber|Offset Number|ADCChannel||||Offset correction is not supported in oversampling mode
Offset|Offset|ADCChannel||0|63|Data offset for regular channel
SamplingTime|Sampling Time|ADCChannel||||Regular Channel x sampling time selection
SAMPLINGTIME_COMMON1|Sampling Time common 1|ADCChannel||||
SAMPLINGTIME_COMMON2|Sampling Time common 2|ADCChannel||||
SamplingTimeCommon1|SamplingTime Common 1|ADCgroup||||Set sampling time common to a group of channels.
Sequencer|Sequencer|ADCgroup||||
SamplingTimeCommon2|SamplingTime Common 2|ADCgroup||||Set sampling time common to a group of channels.
RegHighThreshold|Regular HighThreshold|ADCChannel||||
RegLowThreshold|Regular LowThreshold|ADCChannel||||
RegITMode|Regular ITMode|ADCChannel||||
MonitoredBy|Monitored by|ADCGroup||||Select a watchdog to monitor the channel.
EnableInjectedConversion|Enable Injected Conversions|ADCGroup||||<html> <font color="red"><b>*</b>In case of usage of channels on injected group, ADC frequency should be low than AHB clock frequency /4 for resolution 12 or 10 bits, AHB clock frequency /3 for resolution 8 bits, AHB clock frequency /2 for resolution 6 bits.</font></br></html>
EnableInjectedOversampling|Enable Injected Oversampling|ADC_Injected_ConversionMode||||Enable/Disable Injected Oversampling
